Title: Handle the pointer position of a button event before the button
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: Mouse buttons are sent to the widget under the last handled pointer position, and Button checks hasMouseOver() against the global pointer position, which only mouse-move events update. When the move to the click position was not handled before the press (press and release queued together on a busy system, as with QEMU input), the button got press and release with mouseover=0 and did nothing: "Don't Save" in the quit alert needed several tries.
Change: ui::Manager handles a pointer move to the event position before MouseDown, MouseUp and MouseDoubleClick when the position differs from the current one; when it is the same but a window opened or closed under the still pointer, it picks the widget under the pointer again (catchUpMousePosition).
Scope: all platforms (ui library)
Upstream: candidate
Verification: ABIv11 (AROS One, pool v11-3, 2026-11-16): a temporary trace showed "DBGBTN down 'Don't Save' mouseover=0" and no click before the change; after it mouseover=1 for press and release and the fast click closed the program (quit alert, fast click on New File as well). Second case: two script permission alerts opened one after the other under a still pointer; the click on OK of the second alert did nothing before, and works with the re-pick (v11-3, 2026-11-16).
Removal: when upstream fixes the pointer state for button events.
---
diff --git a/src/ui/manager.cpp b/src/ui/manager.cpp
index e7edd33ae8d75d9aa781d137cc8c49a74f714af5..94584f0dec671e018782478edacd713185eb6e9f 100644
--- a/src/ui/manager.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/manager.cpp
@@ -362,6 +362,7 @@ void Manager::generateMessagesFromSheEvents()
       }
 
       case she::Event::MouseDown: {
+        catchUpMousePosition(sheEvent);
         MouseButtons pressedButton = mouse_buttons_from_she_to_ui(sheEvent);
         m_mouseButtons = (MouseButtons)((int)m_mouseButtons | (int)pressedButton);
         _internal_set_mouse_buttons(m_mouseButtons);
@@ -376,6 +377,7 @@ void Manager::generateMessagesFromSheEvents()
       }
 
       case she::Event::MouseUp: {
+        catchUpMousePosition(sheEvent);
         MouseButtons releasedButton = mouse_buttons_from_she_to_ui(sheEvent);
         m_mouseButtons = (MouseButtons)((int)m_mouseButtons & ~(int)releasedButton);
         _internal_set_mouse_buttons(m_mouseButtons);
@@ -389,6 +391,7 @@ void Manager::generateMessagesFromSheEvents()
       }
 
       case she::Event::MouseDoubleClick: {
+        catchUpMousePosition(sheEvent);
         MouseButtons clickedButton = mouse_buttons_from_she_to_ui(sheEvent);
         // The double click stands in for the second press (Widget converts it into a mouse down),
         // so it must mark the button as pressed for the release that follows.
@@ -434,6 +437,47 @@ void Manager::generateMessagesFromSheEvents()
   }
 }
 
+// A button event carries the pointer position. When no movement to that
+// position has been handled yet (the move event came late, was merged, or the
+// press and release were queued together on a busy system), handle that
+// movement first; when the pointer did not move but a window opened or
+// closed under it, find the widget under it again. The widget under the
+// pointer, its hover state and the position hasMouseOver() reads must match
+// the click, or a button that gets the press and the release does not see
+// the pointer over it and ignores the click.
+void Manager::catchUpMousePosition(const she::Event& sheEvent)
+{
+  if (sheEvent.position() != get_mouse_position()) {
+    _internal_set_mouse_position(sheEvent.position());
+    handleMouseMove(
+      sheEvent.position(),
+      m_mouseButtons,
+      sheEvent.modifiers(),
+      sheEvent.pointerType(),
+      sheEvent.pressure());
+    return;
+  }
+
+  // Same position, but the widgets may have changed under a pointer that did
+  // not move (a dialog opened or closed there): find the widget under it.
+  if (capture_widget)
+    return;
+  mouse_widgets_list.clear();
+  broadcastMouseMessage(mouse_widgets_list);
+  Widget* widget = nullptr;
+  for (auto mouseWidget : mouse_widgets_list) {
+    widget = mouseWidget->pick(sheEvent.position());
+    if (widget)
+      break;
+  }
+  if (widget != mouse_widget) {
+    if (!widget)
+      freeMouse();
+    else
+      setMouse(widget);
+  }
+}
+
 void Manager::handleMouseMove(const gfx::Point& mousePos,
                               MouseButtons mouseButtons,
                               KeyModifiers modifiers,
